// pfodWeb NOTE (verified 2026-07-14): excludes GPIO6/7 - dedicated onboard
// CAN transceiver (CAN1_RX=6/CAN1_TX=7), not general-purpose. Confirmed
// against the official pins_arduino.h in espressif/arduino-esp32:
// https://github.com/espressif/arduino-esp32/blob/master/variants/aslcanx2/pins_arduino.h
// and the vendor's own wiki: https://wiki.autosportlabs.com/ESP32-CAN-X2
// pfodWeb NOTE: GPIO2 tagged "led_low" - confirmed onboard blue status
// LED (LED_BUILTIN=2 in the same pins_arduino.h; Autosport Labs
// ESP32-CAN-X2 official GitHub repo). Active-low polarity confirmed by
// arduino/ping_pong/ping_pong.ino: digitalWrite(LED_BUILTIN, LOW) is
// preceded by Serial.println("MAIN: Enable LED"), HIGH by "MAIN: Disable
// LED" -
// https://github.com/autosportlabs/ESP32-CAN-X2/blob/main/arduino/ping_pong/ping_pong.ino
// GPIO2 pin number cross-confirmed by circuitpython/blink.py: "the LED is
// on IO2" -
// https://github.com/autosportlabs/ESP32-CAN-X2/blob/main/circuitpython/blink.py
